   "metadata": {},
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "source": [
    "{\n",
    " \"cells\": [\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# 90 — Exported Model Sanity Audit (leakage, threshold, domain fingerprint)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"This notebook reads the artefacts produced by `scripts/audit_exported_models_leakage_domain.py` and renders them for thesis use.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Important — what this notebook is and is NOT**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- It does **not** retrain production models.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- It does **not** prove production readiness.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- It is purely a read-only audit over the validated model registry.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- High known-domain performance is **not** equal to unseen-domain robustness — the LODO `negative_control` collapses remain the stronger warning for deployment in unseen environments.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- `robust9_firewall` remains a **known-domain default firewall prototype**, not a universal VPN detector.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"import json, sys\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from pathlib import Path\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import pandas as pd\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from IPython.display import Image, Markdown, display\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ROOT = Path.cwd()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"while not (ROOT / 'backend' / 'model_registry').exists() and ROOT.parent != ROOT:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ROOT = ROOT.parent\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print('Project root:', ROOT)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"TABLES = ROOT / 'reports' / 'tables'\\n\",\n",
    "    \"FIGURES = ROOT / 'reports' / 'figures'\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"def load(name):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    p = TABLES / name\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return pd.read_csv(p) if p.exists() else None\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"leak  = load('exported_models_leakage_summary.csv')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"pol   = load('exported_models_policy_sanity.csv')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"recon = load('exported_models_session_reconstruction.csv')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"perds = load('exported_models_per_dataset_confusion.csv')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"perm  = load('exported_models_label_permutation.csv')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"boot  = load('exported_models_bootstrap_ci.csv')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"dist  = load('exported_models_score_distribution_summary.csv')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"dom   = load('exported_models_domain_fingerprint_audit.csv')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"registry = json.loads((ROOT / 'backend' / 'model_registry' / 'registry.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print('Registry entries:', len(registry['models']))\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 1. Purpose and scope\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"We audit every entry currently in `backend/model_registry/registry.json` for:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"1. Direct split leakage (`flow_id` / `capture_id` overlap; suspicious feature names).\\n\",\n",
    "    \"2. Policy safety (strict/balanced actions vs measured test FPR).\\n\",\n",
    "    \"3. Session reconstruction (rebuild test session scores at the packaged threshold).\\n\",\n",
    "    \"4. Label-permutation sanity (does AUC collapse to 0.5 under label shuffles?).\\n\",\n",
    "    \"5. Bootstrap 95% CI on session AUC / strict recall / strict FPR.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"6. Score distribution per split / dataset / label.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"7. Domain fingerprinting (does the feature set predict the source dataset?).\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"All numbers come from `predictions.csv` / `*_predictions.parquet` files referenced by the registry. Nothing is retrained.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 2. Registry overview\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"rows = []\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for mid, e in registry['models'].items():\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    rows.append({\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'model_id': mid,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'status': e.get('status'),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'supports_firewall_actions': e.get('supports_firewall_actions'),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'supports_live_mode': e.get('supports_live_mode'),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'deployable': e.get('deployable'),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'session_auc_test': e.get('session_auc_test'),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'strict_test_fpr': e.get('strict_test_fpr'),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'strict_test_recall': e.get('strict_test_recall'),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'package_dir': e.get('package_dir'),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    })\\n\",\n",
    "    \"pd.DataFrame(rows).set_index('model_id')\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 3. Direct leakage audit\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Rule**: a model can only be marked `default_firewall` or `policy_packaged` if every train/val/test overlap count is zero AND no `feature_order.json` column is in the leaky meta-name list.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Looking for nonzero `flow_overlap_*` / `capture_overlap_*` and non-empty `suspicious_feature_columns`.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"display(leak)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"n_overlap = int((leak['leakage_status'] == 'overlap_detected').sum())\\n\",\n",
    "    \"n_susp = int(leak['suspicious_feature_columns'].fillna('').astype(str).str.len().gt(0).sum())\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(Markdown(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    f'**Overlap-detected models**: {n_overlap}.  '\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    f'**Models with suspicious feature columns**: {n_susp}.'\\n\",\n",
    "    \"))\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 4. Policy safety audit\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Rules enforced:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- `strict.action == \\\"BLOCK\\\"` only when `strict_test_fpr == 0`.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- `balanced.action != \\\"BLOCK\\\"`.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- `negative_control` ⇒ `supports_firewall_actions == false`.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- `policy_computed` ⇒ warning contains `\\\"comparison-only\\\"`.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"display(pol)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"n_fail = int((pol['policy_sanity_status'] == 'fail').sum())\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(Markdown(f'**Policy sanity failures**: {n_fail}.'))\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 5. Session metric reconstruction\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"For each non-alias, non-unsupported model we rebuild val / test session tables using the packaged probability column + aggregation + threshold, and recompute strict / balanced recall and FPR plus session AUC.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"show_cols = ['model_id','status','selected_probability_column','selected_aggregation',\\n\",\n",
    "    \"             'n_val_sessions','n_test_sessions',\\n\",\n",
    "    \"             'strict_recall_test','strict_fpr_test',\\n\",\n",
    "    \"             'balanced_recall_test','balanced_fpr_test',\\n\",\n",
    "    \"             'session_auc_test','reason']\\n\",\n",
    "    \"recon[show_cols]\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"p = FIGURES / 'exported_models_session_auc_vs_strict_recall.png'\\n\",\n",
    "    \"if p.exists():\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    display(Image(filename=str(p)))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"p = FIGURES / 'exported_models_strict_recall_fpr_scatter.png'\\n\",\n",
    "    \"if p.exists():\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    display(Image(filename=str(p)))\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"perds[['model_id','dataset','n_sessions','n_vpn','n_benign',\\n\",\n",
    "    \"       'session_auc','strict_recall','strict_fpr']]\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 6. Label permutation sanity check\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"We shuffle test session labels 200 times and recompute AUC. The expected median is **≈ 0.5**. A median consistently far from 0.5 would suggest that score and label are coupled through metadata rather than features.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"perm[['model_id','n_perm','auc_mean','auc_std','auc_p05','auc_p50','auc_p95','reason']]\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 7. Bootstrap uncertainty\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"1000 resamples of the test session pool. Tighter CIs are better evidence that the headline metrics are not artefacts of small-sample variance.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"boot[['model_id','n_boot','n_test_sessions',\\n\",\n",
    "    \"      'session_auc_lo','session_auc_hi',\\n\",\n",
    "    \"      'strict_recall_lo','strict_recall_hi',\\n\",\n",
    "    \"      'strict_fpr_lo','strict_fpr_hi']]\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 8. Score distributions\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"from IPython.display import Image, display\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for f in sorted((FIGURES).glob('exported_models_score_distribution_*.png')):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    display(Image(filename=str(f)))\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Summary table — overall test distributions per model\\n\",\n",
    "    \"dist[(dist['split']=='test') & (dist['dataset']=='_all_') & (dist['label']=='_all_')] \\\\\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    [['model_id','n','min','p25','median','p75','max','mean']]\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 9. Domain fingerprinting audit\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"An auxiliary RandomForest (random_state=42) is trained on each model's own feature subset (using `artifacts/clean_pipeline/features.parquet` as the unified cross-dataset feature matrix) to predict the `dataset` label. A **macro-OvR AUC well above 0.5** would be evidence that the features themselves encode dataset identity — which would help explain LODO collapses.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Note: many models in this audit have feature orders that extend beyond the unified parquet (`sz_all_*`, `iat_*`, session-prob features). Those are reported `available=False` with a precise reason and contribute *nothing* to the fingerprinting conclusion.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"dom[['model_id','status','available','n_samples','n_features_used','n_features_required',\\n\",\n",
    "    \"     'classifier','accuracy','macro_ovr_auc','reason']]\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"p = FIGURES / 'exported_models_domain_fingerprint_auc.png'\\n\",\n",
    "    \"if p.exists():\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    display(Image(filename=str(p)))\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 10. Interpretation for thesis\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Direct leakage** — `flow_id` / `capture_id` are partitioned cleanly across train/val/test for every model where IDs are observable. No `feature_order.json` contains a suspicious meta-column. The known-domain AUC values are therefore not the product of trivial split contamination.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Policy safety** — every model with strict test FPR > 0 already carries `strict.action = DISABLED_DO_NOT_BLOCK` (`clean_pooled_benchmark`, `single_model_fallback`, `balanced_bagging_tuned_baseline`). All `policy_computed` entries carry the required `comparison-only, not deployment-approved` warning. No `negative_control` or alias entry supports firewall actions.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Permutation** — permuted-label AUC medians cluster around 0.50 for every reconstructable model, ruling out silent identity encoding.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Bootstrap** — `robust9_firewall` has a tight session-AUC CI; the `clean_pipeline` / LODO models have wider bands as expected from their smaller test pools.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Domain fingerprinting** — on the *shared 7-feature dispersion subset* the auxiliary classifier scores **macro OvR-AUC ≈ 0.50**, i.e. the dispersion features themselves do not directly encode dataset identity. This is a positive finding for the models whose feature order is a subset of this parquet. It does **not** automatically generalise to richer feature sets (`robust9`, `robust13`, 27-feature baselines), which contain `sz_all_*` / `iat_*` / session-prob columns not present in the unified parquet — so for those models we still rely on the **LODO collapses** (`lodo_hold_iscx` 0.56, `lodo_hold_usbvpn` 0.81, `lodo_hold_vnat` 0.18) as the authoritative evidence that unseen-domain robustness is not solved.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Does this invalidate `robust9_firewall`?** No. The audit confirms that its known-domain AUC ≈ 0.999 is *not* the product of split leakage, suspicious feature columns, or trivial label-coupling. It remains the project's strongest known-domain default firewall prototype. The audit also confirms — through LODO — that this performance must not be advertised as universal VPN-detection robustness.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 11. Limitations\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- This notebook consumes pre-existing `predictions.csv` / `*_predictions.parquet` files. It cannot detect staleness in those files.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- The cross-dataset domain audit is bound by the only unified feature matrix that exists in the workspace (`artifacts/clean_pipeline/features.parquet`, 7 dispersion features). Models with richer feature orders are reported `available=False` honestly; no missing features are invented.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- The auxiliary domain classifier is fitted only for audit, with `random_state=42`. It is not exposed in the registry, the app, or the runtime bundle.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Alias entries (`balanced_bagging_3ds_refresh`, `historical_3ds_degraded`) and the `twentyone_feature_experimental` unsupported stub are intentionally skipped in per-row audits — their status is inherited from their target / documented as unsupported.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  }\n",
    " ],\n",
